Every visually meaningful element gets an ID and an implementation decision.

3. Token extraction happens too early

The proposal assumes the mockup can be reduced to tokens before understanding its visual construction.

That is dangerous.

A fantasy UI's appearance is often dominated by relationships, not isolated values:

border thickness relative to panel size;

highlight intensity relative to background;

banner overlap relative to frame;

image crop relative to ornamental frame;

shadow softness relative to material;

typography scale relative to available content area.

Extracting #123456, border-radius: 8px, gap: 12px is not reproducing the design language.

Fix: separate:

structural measurements;

semantic design tokens;

effect/material parameters.

4. “Canonical spec per generated asset” does not protect the component

The failure wasn't primarily an asset-generation failure.

V17's problem was composition.

You can have a perfect goblin illustration and still produce a terrible modal.

The workflow therefore overweights asset provenance and underweights composition acceptance.

Fix: the component itself needs a canonical visual spec and measurable checkpoints.

